§ `s 2(1) -- am I an employee`

#ASSERT `Am I an employee under the Employment Act` `an ordinary employee`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I an employee under the Employment Act` `a domestic worker`

§ `ss 8, 10, 11 -- notice`

-- A 1-day term is void for a ten-year employee (s 8), leaving s 10(3)(d): 28 days. For a new starter it equals
-- the statutory minimum and stands. A silent contract at 3 years: s 10(3)(c), 14 days.
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a mean contract of 1 day` `a new starter` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many days of notice am I owed` `a silent contract` `three years in` EQUALS 14

#ASSERT `How much must I be paid in lieu of notice` 200 `a mean contract of 1 day` `ten years in` EQUALS 5600

§ `s 13(2) -- absence`

-- A reasonable excuse never communicated still makes out limb (b).
#ASSERT NOT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` `two days away, no leave, no excuse`
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` `three days away, no leave, no excuse`
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having broken my contract by being absent` `ten days away with an excuse never mentioned`

§ `s 15 -- danger`

#ASSERT `May I leave without notice because of danger` `an immediate threat of violence`
#ASSERT NOT `May I leave without notice because of danger` `a threat that is not immediate`

§ `s 14 -- dismissal and suspension`

#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer dismiss me without notice for misconduct` `misconduct found without an inquiry`

#ASSERT `Is my suspension without pay as a penalty lawful` `a week's suspension after an inquiry`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my suspension without pay as a penalty lawful` `eight days' suspension after an inquiry`

#ASSERT NOT `Is my suspension pending inquiry within the time allowed` `ten days suspended, misconduct found`

#ASSERT `What is the least I must be paid for my suspension pending inquiry` `ten days suspended, misconduct found` EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `What is the least I must be paid for my suspension pending inquiry` `ten days suspended, no misconduct found` EQUALS 1000

-- The 6-month qualification bites only on a manager dismissed properly; one sacked on the spot may claim at once.
#ASSERT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` `a manager given notice after 6 months`
#ASSERT NOT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` `a manager given notice in month 3`
#ASSERT `Can I claim for wrongful dismissal` `a manager sacked on the spot in month 3`

§ `s 45 -- retrenchment benefit`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit` 1.5 TRUE EQUALS `none -- under 2 years of continuous service (s 45)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a retrenchment benefit` 2 TRUE EQUALS `not decided by this Act -- it depends on my contract or a collective agreement`

§ `ss 21-24 -- when I must be paid`

#ASSERT `Was I paid late` `my salary after I was dismissed` 4
#ASSERT NOT `Was I paid late` `my salary after I was dismissed` 3
#ASSERT `Was I paid late` `my overtime pay for a salary period` 15

-- s 21(1) as a duty: salary paid on day 5 of the 7 fulfils it.
#TRACE `my employer's duty to pay my salary` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my salary for the salary period` AT 5

§ `ss 27, 29, 32 -- deductions`

#ASSERT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `for absence from work` `no consent`
#ASSERT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `for house accommodation supplied by my employer` `standing consent`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer make this deduction from my salary` `for house accommodation supplied by my employer` `withdrawn consent`

-- s 29: the ceiling is the lesser of the loss (900) and a quarter of 2,000 (500).
#ASSERT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` `a 400 deduction for a 900 loss, after showing cause` `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` `a 600 deduction for a 900 loss, after showing cause` `the proportions as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Can my employer deduct this amount for damage or loss I caused` `a 10 deduction without a chance to show cause` `the proportions as the Act states them`

#ASSERT NOT `Are the deductions from my salary this period within the overall limit` 1200 2000 FALSE `the proportions as the Act states them`

§ `ss 35, 37, 38 -- rest days and overtime`

-- A mixed worker whose workman time never reached half is not a workman, and falls under the $2,600 cap.
#ASSERT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` `a labourer on 4500` `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT NOT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` `a labourer on 4501` `the caps as the Act states them`
#ASSERT `Do the rest day, hours and overtime rules cover me` `a mostly clerical mixed worker on 2600` `the caps as the Act states them`

-- Fourth Schedule: 12 x 2,288 / (52 x 44) = 12 an hour; 2 hours at 1.5 x 12 = 36.
#ASSERT `What is the least I must be paid for my overtime` 2 (`monthly` 2288) EQUALS 36

-- s 37: half a day at own request = 50; 1 day + 2 hours at 1.5 x 12.5 = 137.5; at the employer's request, no
-- agreed hours (deemed 8), 1.5 hours over rounds up to 2: 2 days + 37.5 = 237.5.
#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` `four hours at my own request` EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` `ten hours at my own request` EQUALS 137.5
#ASSERT `What must I be paid for working on my rest day` `nine and a half hours at my employer's request, no agreed hours` EQUALS 237.5

§ `ss 88A, 89 -- leave`

-- Six months in the first year: 7 x 6 / 12 = 3.5, rounded up to 4 (s 88A(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `How many days of annual leave do I get` `a full first year` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `How many days of annual leave do I get` `a full tenth year` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `How many days of annual leave do I get` `six months into the first year` EQUALS 4

#ASSERT `What must I be paid for annual leave not taken when I am dismissed` 5 100 TRUE EQUALS 0

-- At 4 months in hospital for 30 days: the lesser of 30 and 8 + 30.
#ASSERT `How many days of paid sick leave can I take in the year` `six months in, outpatient` EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `How many days of paid sick leave can I take in the year` `six months in, ten days in hospital` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `How many days of paid sick leave can I take in the year` `four months in, thirty days in hospital` EQUALS 30

§ `ss 76, 80, 81, 83 -- maternity`

-- 8 weeks = 56 days at 100: 5,600; halved without the s 80 notices.
#ASSERT `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` `a qualifying confinement` EQUALS `paid` 5600
#ASSERT `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` `a confinement after 2 months' service` EQUALS `nothing is payable`
#ASSERT `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` `a third child from a third confinement` EQUALS `nothing is payable`
#ASSERT `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` `a confinement with no notice given` EQUALS `paid` 2800
#ASSERT `How much maternity pay must my employer give me` `a confinement in 2014` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding -- confinement before 22 August 2015`

#ASSERT `Is the notice of dismissal I was given unlawful because of my maternity absence` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 95A -- key employment terms`

#ASSERT `Did my employer give me my key employment terms as section 95A requires` `key terms on day 14` EQUALS `my employer complied`
#ASSERT `Did my employer give me my key employment terms as section 95A requires` `key terms on day 15` EQUALS `my employer failed to comply`
#ASSERT `Did my employer give me my key employment terms as section 95A requires` `a contract from 2015` EQUALS `section 95A does not apply to me`

§ `s 96A and the Notification -- retrenchment reporting`

#ASSERT `Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` `a redundancy notice from an employer of 40` EQUALS `yes, my employer must report it`
#ASSERT `Must my employer report my retrenchment to the Commissioner` `a redundancy notice from an employer of 9` EQUALS `no report is required`

-- Notice on day 3 (Thursday 4 November 2021): working days 4, 7, 8, 9, 10 -> day 10. With day 7 an illustrative
-- holiday: 4, 8, 9, 10, 11 -> day 11.
#ASSERT `By which day must my employer report my retrenchment` 3 EMPTY EQUALS 10
